-- =============================================================================================
-- BizApps Tasks v1.14.x -- Metadata_Sync (Meetings)
-- =============================================================================================
-- Generated by `mj sync push --dir metadata --ci` (MJ CLI 6.2.1) against a database built from
-- migrations ONLY: MJ core v6.2.1, then bizapps-common, -accounting, -orders, -contracts and this
-- app at their released state (Tasks v1.13.0), then this app's migrations at `next` (Meetings).
--
-- CREATED (create-only):
--   * 5 row-level security filters (Tasks: Visible Meetings, Rows Of Visible Meetings, Visible
--     Meeting Links, Visible Meeting Series, Visible Meeting Series Attendees).
--   * Credential type "Video Provider OAuth" (same ID and name bizapps-committees ships).
--   * The Meetings application, and the Tasks settings DefaultCalendarProviderName and
--     SharedCalendarMailbox (both empty: calendar sync stays off).
--   * AI prompts "Tasks: Meeting Notes from Transcript" and "Tasks: Draft Meeting Agenda", with
--     their templates, template contents and 16 template params.
--   * 7 meeting agenda item types, 5 meeting types, 3 video providers (all shipped inactive).
--   * Scheduled job type "Meeting Series Materialization" and its daily job (03:00 UTC, Active).
--
-- UPDATED (only while the CodeGen default is still there):
--   * The UI role's permissions on Meetings, Meeting Series, Meeting Series Attendees, Meeting
--     Attendees, Meeting Agenda Items, Meeting Notes and Meeting Links: create/update(/delete)
--     plus the read filter above. Skipped where the permission already has a read filter.
--   * Meeting Agenda Items.ParentID Configuration (hierarchy). Skipped where one is set.
--
-- CREATE-ONLY: each create is guarded on its ID or its natural key (Name, Code, Path, DriverClass,
-- ApplicationID+Name, TemplateID+Name, TemplateID+TypeID), and the push log's update branch is cut,
-- so a host's own edits survive and a re-run writes nothing.
--
-- NOT INCLUDED: the push also creates the ML training pipelines, ML model, scoring binding, record
-- process and its scoring job under metadata/ml-*, record-processes (their files changed only in
-- sync blocks this release). No earlier Tasks seed ships them, and this one does not change that;
-- no Meetings record depends on them.
--
-- TRANSFORMS: the filters' PlatformVariants field (PostgreSQL text; MemberJunction 6.3+) is left
-- out: MJ 6.2.1, this line's MJ, has no such column. FilterText is the T-SQL text. Core references
-- use ${mjSchema}, this app's schema ${flyway:defaultSchema}; string values untouched. Idempotent.
-- =============================================================================================

